# Standalone build copy for EAS.
#
# ios/ IS COMMITTED here on purpose. The widget extension is created by a config
# plugin during prebuild, and EAS resolves signing credentials on the client
# BEFORE upload — so a plugin-generated target is invisible to it and never gets
# a provisioning profile. Committing the generated Xcode project means EAS sees
# both targets upfront and can provision the extension.
#
# Leading slashes matter: an unanchored ios/ also matches modules/*/ios/, which
# holds the native Swift source.

/node_modules/
/ios/Pods/
/ios/build/
/ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
/ios/*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
/android/
/.expo/
/dist/
.DS_Store
*.log
